# Sandcastle environment template.
#
# ===========================================================================
# ON A LOCAL MAC WITH A CLAUDE PRO/MAX SUBSCRIPTION: YOU NEED NOTHING HERE.
# Every key below is OPTIONAL — leave them all blank and run. The default
# models are all Claude (see models.ts) and use the `claude` CLI's own login;
# `gh` is mounted from your host auth. Only fill a key in if a comment below
# says your specific setup needs it (a non-Claude provider, a VPS with no
# `claude login`, or a test database).
# ===========================================================================
#
# Two valid locations (orchestrator reads both; project-local wins):
#   1. <project-root>/.env       — per-project override
#   2. ~/.config/sandcastle/.env — host-level default, shared across every
#                                  project and worktree on this machine.
#                                  Recommended for KIMI/GLM keys and the pool
#                                  you want to set once.
#
# Override the host-level path with `$SANDCASTLE_ENV_FILE=...` if you need
# a custom layout (e.g. piping from 1Password / sops).
#
# Do NOT commit a real .env — `.sandcastle/.gitignore` excludes it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Kimi (kimi.com) — OPTIONAL. The default models are all Claude
# (models.ts), so leave this empty unless you explicitly pass
# `--provider kimi` or set a kimi-* model id. Only then is it required.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
KIMI_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GLM (z.ai Coding Plan) — only required if you pass `--provider glm` or use
# a glm-* model id. Safe to leave empty otherwise.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GLM_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Account pool — the address of the pool (CLIProxyAPI) every agent draws
# Claude from, and the word sent as its key. Set both in the host-level
# ~/.config/sandcastle/.env, never in a shell export: the loop ignores a
# launching shell's copy. Forwarded into every sandbox and logged by name.
# Inside Docker, `localhost` is the container itself; use the pool's
# Tailscale name. ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN outranks CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN, so
# no subscription token is needed once these are set.
#
# Never set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY for the loop: it bills the paid API instead of
# the subscription, even when a login exists.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=
ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub — used by the HOST only (claiming tickets, labels, the run PR).
# It is never forwarded into a sandbox and ~/.config/gh is never mounted:
# no agent holds a GitHub key (spec #1334). The host reads each ticket and
# hands its text to the prompts. A `gh auth login` on the host also works.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GH_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cross-host issue lease + lane sync — OPTIONAL. All default OFF;
# a single-host loop needs none of these and behaves byte-for-byte as before.
#
# SANDCASTLE_CROSS_HOST_LEASE  set to 1/true to enable the per-issue lease so
#   two machines running loops against the SAME repo/queue never double-work an
#   issue (each issue is claimed via a lock ref on origin). OFF by default.
#   Requires push access to origin (the lock refs live under refs/locks/*).
#
# SANDCASTLE_CROSS_HOST_SYNC  set to 1/true to enable cross-host LANE SYNC —
#   each host publishes its integration branch to a lane ref on origin and pulls
#   its peers' lanes in at the start of each cycle, so two machines SHARE the
#   code they produce. OFF by default. REQUIRES SANDCASTLE_CROSS_HOST_LEASE=1
#   (sharing code without the per-issue lock is unsafe — the loop refuses to
#   start if sync is on while the lease is off). Requires push access to origin
#   (lanes live under refs/sandcastle/lanes/*).
#
# SANDCASTLE_HOST_ID  identifies THIS host when several machines run loops
#   against the same repo/queue, so leases + lanes can be attributed to a host.
#   Defaults to a sanitized `os.hostname()`. Set it only if two hosts share a
#   hostname or you want a stable, human-friendly id. Value is lower-cased and
#   reduced to a branch-safe fragment ([a-z0-9._-], max 40 chars).
#
# SANDCASTLE_LOCK_TTL_SEC  how long (in seconds) an issue lease is held before
#   it may be reclaimed by another host. Positive integer; defaults to 900
#   (15 min). Garbage / zero / negative values fall back to the default.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SANDCASTLE_CROSS_HOST_LEASE=
SANDCASTLE_CROSS_HOST_SYNC=
SANDCASTLE_HOST_ID=
SANDCASTLE_LOCK_TTL_SEC=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LIVE STATUS PUSH (mission-control feed). Both must be set or push is OFF and
# the loop behaves exactly as before.
#
# Why this exists: status.json and the git status ref are both PULL surfaces,
# and NEITHER ever carries a run's terminal state or its final cost — those are
# committed after the last publish. That is why a finished run kept rendering
# as "running" long after it exited, and why a dashboard reported a third of
# what a run actually spent. Pushing from the status store's commit() closes
# both gaps, because the terminal write goes out like any other.
#
# SANDCASTLE_STATUS_PUSH_URL    full URL of the ingest endpoint, e.g.
#   https://control.example.com/ingest
# SANDCASTLE_STATUS_PUSH_TOKEN  shared secret sent as `Authorization: Bearer`.
#   NOT the dashboard's browser password — a separate machine-to-machine token.
#
# Delivery is best-effort by design: fire-and-forget, coalesced, one request in
# flight at a time, and it can never throw into or block a run.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SANDCASTLE_STATUS_PUSH_URL=
SANDCASTLE_STATUS_PUSH_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SANDCASTLE_IMPLEMENTER_TIMEOUT_SEC  implementer idle-timeout in seconds;
#   raise it for projects whose inline e2e can exceed the 20-min/1200s default.
#   Positive integer; the CLI --implementer-timeout-sec flag overrides it.
#   Leave blank to use the 1200s default.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SANDCASTLE_IMPLEMENTER_TIMEOUT_SEC=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# First-pass reviewer escalation. Normally the reviewer's FIRST pass runs on
# the cheap default model; these knobs make it escalate to the reviewer's
# stronger escalation model on pass 1 when the change is large or sensitive —
# one strong pass beats a cheap miss. Small, ordinary diffs are unaffected.
#
# SANDCASTLE_REVIEW_ESCALATE_DIFF_LINES  added+deleted line count at/above which
#   the first pass escalates. Positive integer; defaults to 400. Garbage / zero
#   / negative values fall back to the default.
#   NOTE: 0 (or negative) does NOT disable escalation — it falls back to the
#   default 400. To effectively disable the line rule, set a very high number.
# SANDCASTLE_REVIEW_ESCALATE_PATHS  comma-separated globs; if any changed file
#   matches, the first pass escalates regardless of size. Defaults to DB
#   migration files/dirs only: **/migrations/**,*.sql. Leave blank for that
#   default; set your own generic globs (NOT project business paths) to widen.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SANDCASTLE_REVIEW_ESCALATE_DIFF_LINES=
SANDCASTLE_REVIEW_ESCALATE_PATHS=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test database (optional). Set `testDatabase` in .sandcastle/project.json
# (see project.example.json) to give every sandbox its own copy of a template
# Postgres database; the host needs `psql`. Environment knobs:
#   SANDCASTLE_TEST_DB_URL        point every sandbox at THIS database (no
#                                 per-job clone). Must be a local disposable
#                                 Postgres, never port 5432.
#   SANDCASTLE_TEST_PG_PORT       port of the default local test Postgres
#                                 (default 55432).
#   SANDCASTLE_TEST_DB_ADMIN_URL  host-side admin connection override.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SANDCASTLE_TEST_DB_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Screenshot storage (Cloudflare R2) — where the browser check files its
# receipt picture. A machine missing these takes the screenshot, fails to file
# it, marks the record `picture not stored`, and SHIPS ANYWAY. That is
# deliberate (the proof is the check, not the photo) — but it means a machine
# set up without these looks like policy working as designed while filing
# nothing forever. Copy the values from a machine that already has them.
#
# Use the SEPARATE screen-check bucket and its narrowly-scoped key. Never the
# bucket holding encrypted customer-document backups.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_SCREEN_CHECK_BUCKET=
R2_SCREEN_CHECK_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_SCREEN_CHECK_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The loop's only way to shout: an ntfy topic. Every "fail loudly" clause in
# the screen-check design pushes here. Unset means the push is skipped and the
# skip is logged — so the loop runs completely silent.
#
# DEFERRED as of 2026-08-15 (issue #913): the owner watches runs live rather
# than overnight, so no topic is set on ANY machine today. Set this before the
# loop is ever run unattended again.
#
# The topic the rest of this repo already uses is documented in
# docs/reference/vps-setup.md under "Notifications".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
NTFY_TOPIC=
